"""Two-peer lockstep run for netplay co-op.

Pair mode (default) launches a host and a joiner of the netplay build as two
hidden, private, bounded processes over loopback UDP. Each peer:

  * runs in its own run directory (<out>/host, <out>/join) as working
    directory, so pikmin_settings.conf is a private copy (seeded from
    --config / --config-host / --config-join), the memory card goes to
    NECTAR_SAVE_DIR=<run>/save and the game files are reached through a
    <run>/assets junction (symlink off Windows) to --assets;
  * plays its own scripted input, generated by gen_inputs.py with its own
    seed and passed as --netplay-input <run>/input.pkni;
  * runs unthrottled (PIKMIN_NETPLAY_UNTHROTTLED=1, unless --throttled) with
    SDL_AUDIODRIVER=dummy, and stops after --ticks session ticks
    (PIKMIN_NETPLAY_EXIT_AFTER_TICKS), writing a per-tick state-hash log;
  * binds 127.0.0.1 only (PIKMIN_NETPLAY_UDP_BIND).

Both peers boot through the co-op direct boot (every netplay session does).
Only the spawned processes are ever killed.

Expectations (--expect):
  sync    both exit 0, identical hash logs over every tick, no desync line,
          the "[NETPLAY] coop_active=1 navis=2" marker on both, and real
          gameplay: the navi hash takes many distinct values and both
          captains move (the [netplay-navi] position lines).
  refuse  both exit 4 with a "[netplay] handshake refused:" line.
  desync  both exit 5 after a desync, and each writes a two-sided
          desync-report.txt (both peers' sub-hashes) and its session input
          log. Pair it with a TEST ONLY perturbation, for example
          --env-join PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_KNOBS=1 PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_DESYNC_NUDGE=1500:navi:1
          (--desync-nudge 1500:navi:1 sets exactly that on the joiner).

ICE (--ice): the peers use --netplay-host-ice / --netplay-join-ice instead
of the UDP switches, and this script carries the connection codes through
files: the host writes its offer (--netplay-code-out), the joiner is started
with --netplay-join-ice @<that file> and writes its answer, which is copied
into the host's --netplay-answer-in file. Each peer's launcher run folder is
<run>/netplay/run-*. By default PIKMIN_NETPLAY_STUN=none and
PIKMIN_NETPLAY_ICE_BIND=127.0.0.1 (loopback host candidates only, no network
beyond this PC); --stun/--ice-bind change that. Settings adoption: with
--ice, --config-join values that differ from the host's are adopted from the
offer, so --expect sync still holds (the joiner's settings file is checked to
be unchanged).

Impairment: --latency-ms/--jitter-ms/--loss-pct use the in-exe lossy adapter
on the GekkoNet channel (PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_*); --proxy "lat:jit:loss" puts
the netplay_impair_proxy between the peers instead (every datagram, both
directions, handshake included).

VS (--mode vs): both peers get --netplay-mode vs (plus --vs-map FILE when
given) and play the VS script of gen_inputs.py (--vs-starts, --vs-yaw-host/
--vs-yaw-join, --vs-path) instead of the field script. --expect sync then
also wants, on both peers and with the same text: the "[VS] match over" lines
(winner, score, pieces and tick), a scoring line, the "[VS] end screen" choice
lines, a VS mode column that changes, and with --vs-matches N at least N match
starts ("[VS] piece kind 5" once per match). Use a short match:
--env PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_KNOBS=1 PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_VS_MATCH_SECONDS=60.

Ext inputs (Bomb, Lock-On, Charge/Swarm, cursor rotate): --ext gives both
peers seeded ext events (gen_inputs --ext), --ext-events[-host|-join] explicit
ones (gen_inputs --ext-events); either turns on PIKMIN_NETPLAY_DEBUG_EXT=1.
The sim's "[EXT]" lines must then be identical on both peers, and
--require-ext KIND[,...] wants each KIND on both: input, rotate, bomb, lock,
charge, release (per captain, --require-ext-navis) and explode (any).
Enable the mods with --config bombControl=1 lockOn=1 charge=1.

Examples:
    py tools/netplay/run_pair.py --exe <build>/bin/nectar.exe --assets <assets> \\
        --ticks 3000 --out run/pair1
    py tools/netplay/run_pair.py ... --out run/refuse-fps --expect refuse \\
        --config-join fpsMode=1
    py tools/netplay/run_pair.py ... --out run/refuse-exe --expect refuse --exe-join-variant

Single peer against a remote machine (--peer-only host|join). The peer runs
the same private run directory, scripted input and tick bound, but binds
--bind (default 127.0.0.1; a two-PC test passes 0.0.0.0, which may raise the
OS firewall prompt on first use) and talks to --remote. Run the host on one
PC and the joiner on the other with the same exe, --ticks and --netplay-seed:

    host PC: py tools/netplay/run_pair.py --peer-only host --exe ... --assets ... \\
                 --ticks 3000 --out run/lan-host --bind 0.0.0.0 --port 48810
    join PC: py tools/netplay/run_pair.py --peer-only join --exe ... --assets ... \\
                 --ticks 3000 --out run/lan-join --bind 0.0.0.0 --remote <host-ip>:48810

Compare the two hashes.txt afterwards with compare_hashes.py.

Two PCs over ICE (--peer-only with --ice): the host writes
<out>/host/offer.txt and waits for <out>/host/answer-in.txt; the joiner reads
the offer from --offer FILE and writes <out>/join/answer.txt. Carry the offer
to the joiner's PC and the answer back to the host's answer-in.txt by any
means (a shared folder, scp). --ice-bind any is needed between two PCs, and
--stun public (public STUN) across the internet without a VPN:

    host PC: py tools/netplay/run_pair.py --peer-only host --ice --ice-bind any --stun public \\
                 --exe ... --assets ... --ticks 3000 --out run/ice-host
    join PC: py tools/netplay/run_pair.py --peer-only join --ice --ice-bind any --stun public \\
                 --exe ... --assets ... --ticks 3000 --out run/ice-join --offer <copied offer.txt>
"""

import argparse
import hashlib
import os
import re
import shutil
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

try:
    import _winapi
except ImportError:  # not Windows: a symlink is used instead
    _winapi = None

TOOLS = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
HASH_COLUMNS = ["total", "navi", "piki", "teki", "item", "world", "rng", "mode"]
# A netplay or harness switch left in the caller's environment must not leak in.
SCRUB_PREFIXES = ("PIKMIN_NETPLAY_", "PIKMIN_INPUT_", "PIKMIN_STATE_HASH_", "PIKMIN_COOP")


def parse_kv(items, what):
    out = {}
    for item in items or []:
        if "=" not in item:
            raise SystemExit(f"--{what} needs key=value, got {item!r}")
        key, value = item.split("=", 1)
        out[key.strip()] = value.strip()
    return out


def link_assets(target, link):
    if link.exists():
        return
    if _winapi is not None:
        _winapi.CreateJunction(str(target), str(link))
    else:
        os.symlink(str(target), str(link), target_is_directory=True)


def sha256_file(path):
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(1 << 20), b""):
            h.update(chunk)
    return h.hexdigest()


def gen_inputs(ticks, seed, out, extra=None):
    subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(TOOLS / "gen_inputs.py"), "--ticks", str(ticks), "--seed", str(seed),
                    "--out", str(out)] + (extra or []), check=True, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL)


def prepare_run(run, assets, config, ticks, seed, gen_extra=None):
    run.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    link_assets(assets, run / "assets")
    (run / "save").mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    conf = run / "pikmin_settings.conf"
    if config:
        with open(conf, "w") as f:
            for key, value in sorted(config.items()):
                f.write(f"{key} = {value}\n")
    elif conf.exists():
        conf.unlink()
    for stale in ("hashes.txt", "native.log"):
        if (run / stale).exists():
            (run / stale).unlink()
    pkni = run / "input.pkni"
    # A few hundred spare records: a peer's input for frame F is record F - d.
    gen_inputs(ticks + 600, seed, pkni, gen_extra)
    return pkni


def launch(exe, run, exe_args, env_extra, unthrottled, ticks):
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if not k.upper().startswith(SCRUB_PREFIXES)}
    env.update(
        SDL_AUDIODRIVER="dummy",
        NECTAR_SAVE_DIR=str((run / "save").resolve()),
        PIKMIN_STATE_HASH_LOG=str((run / "hashes.txt").resolve()),
        PIKMIN_NETPLAY_EXIT_AFTER_TICKS=str(ticks),
        PIKMIN_NETPLAY_DEBUG_NAVI_POS="1",
    )
    if unthrottled:
        env["PIKMIN_NETPLAY_UNTHROTTLED"] = "1"
    env.update(env_extra)
    startup = None
    if sys.platform == "win32":
        startup = subprocess.STARTUPINFO()
        startup.dwFlags |= subprocess.STARTF_USESHOWWINDOW
        startup.wShowWindow = 0
    out = open(run / "native.log", "w")
    proc = subprocess.Popen([str(Path(exe).resolve())] + exe_args, cwd=str(run), env=env, startupinfo=startup,
                            stdout=out, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
    return proc, out


def wait_all(procs, timeout):
    """Waits for every (name, proc); kills only these on timeout. Returns rc by name."""
    deadline = time.time() + timeout
    rcs = {}
    for name, proc in procs:
        left = max(1.0, deadline - time.time())
        try:
            rcs[name] = proc.wait(timeout=left)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            print(f"run_pair: {name} timed out, killing pid {proc.pid}")
            proc.kill()
            try:
                rcs[name] = proc.wait(timeout=30)
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                rcs[name] = 124
    return rcs


def read_hashes(path):
    rows = {}
    try:
        with open(path, "r", errors="replace") as f:
            for line in f:
                cols = line.split()
                if len(cols) != 1 + len(HASH_COLUMNS):
                    continue
                try:
                    rows[int(cols[0])] = cols[1:]
                except ValueError:
                    continue
    except OSError:
        pass
    return rows


def compare_hashes(a, b):
    """(identical, ticks compared, first differing tick, differing columns)."""
    ta, tb = read_hashes(a), read_hashes(b)
    if not ta or len(ta) != len(tb):
        return False, min(len(ta), len(tb)), None, [f"line counts {len(ta)} vs {len(tb)}"]
    for tick in sorted(ta):
        if tb.get(tick) != ta[tick]:
            cols = [c for c, x, y in zip(HASH_COLUMNS, ta[tick], tb.get(tick, [""] * 8)) if x != y]
            return False, len(ta), tick, cols
    return True, len(ta), None, []


NAVI_RE = re.compile(r"\[netplay-navi\] tick=(\d+) navi=(\d+) pos=\(([-\d.]+) ([-\d.]+) ([-\d.]+)\)")


def navi_travel(log_text):
    """Per captain: (samples, path length, max distance from the first sample)."""
    pos = {}
    for m in NAVI_RE.finditer(log_text):
        pos.setdefault(int(m.group(2)), []).append(tuple(float(m.group(i)) for i in (3, 5)))
    out = {}
    for navi, pts in pos.items():
        path = sum(((x1 - x0) ** 2 + (z1 - z0) ** 2) ** 0.5 for (x0, z0), (x1, z1) in zip(pts, pts[1:]))
        far = max((((x - pts[0][0]) ** 2 + (z - pts[0][1]) ** 2) ** 0.5 for x, z in pts), default=0.0)
        out[navi] = (len(pts), path, far)
    return out


def lines_with(text, needle):
    return [ln for ln in text.splitlines() if needle in ln]


def peer_summary(name, run, rc):
    text = (run / "native.log").read_text(errors="replace") if (run / "native.log").exists() else ""
    hashes = read_hashes(run / "hashes.txt")
    distinct_navi = len({row[1] for row in hashes.values()})
    travel = navi_travel(text)
    info = {
        "rc": rc,
        "text": text,
        "ticks": len(hashes),
        "distinct_navi": distinct_navi,
        "distinct_total": len({row[0] for row in hashes.values()}),
        "travel": travel,
        "desync": lines_with(text, "desync detected"),
        "refused": lines_with(text, "handshake refused:"),
        "marker": lines_with(text, "[NETPLAY] coop_active="),
        "vs_over": lines_with(text, "[VS] match over"),
        "vs_end": lines_with(text, "[VS] end screen:"),
        "vs_score": [ln for ln in text.splitlines() if re.match(r"\[VS\] P[12] \+\d+", ln)],
        "vs_matches": len(lines_with(text, "[VS] piece kind 5")),
        "distinct_mode": len({row[7] for row in hashes.values()}),
        "started": lines_with(text, "[netplay] session started:"),
    }
    print(f"run_pair: {name}: exit={rc} hash ticks={info['ticks']} distinct navi hashes={distinct_navi} "
          f"distinct totals={info['distinct_total']}")
    for line in info["started"] + info["marker"] + info["refused"] + info["desync"][:3]:
        print(f"run_pair: {name}:   {line.strip()}")
    for navi, (n, path, far) in sorted(travel.items()):
        print(f"run_pair: {name}:   captain {navi}: {n} position samples, path {path:.1f}, farthest {far:.1f} "
              f"from the first sample")
    for line in info["vs_score"][:6] + info["vs_over"] + info["vs_end"]:
        print(f"run_pair: {name}:   {line.strip()}")
    if info["vs_matches"]:
        print(f"run_pair: {name}:   VS matches started: {info['vs_matches']}, distinct mode hashes: "
              f"{info['distinct_mode']}")
    for line in lines_with(text, "[netplay] exit after") + lines_with(text, "[netplay] wall="):
        print(f"run_pair: {name}:   {line.strip()}")
    print(f"run_pair: {name}: log {run / 'native.log'}")
    return info


def check_sync(h, j, args):
    ok = True
    if h["rc"] != 0 or j["rc"] != 0:
        print(f"run_pair: FAIL: exit codes host={h['rc']} join={j['rc']} (want 0 0)")
        ok = False
    same, n, tick, cols = compare_hashes(args.out / "host" / "hashes.txt", args.out / "join" / "hashes.txt")
    if same and n == args.ticks:
        print(f"run_pair: hashes identical on both peers over {n} ticks")
    else:
        print(f"run_pair: FAIL: hashes differ or are short: {n} ticks compared (want {args.ticks}), "
              f"first differing tick {tick}, columns {cols}")
        ok = False
    for name, p in (("host", h), ("join", j)):
        if p["desync"]:
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} logged {len(p['desync'])} desync lines")
            ok = False
        if not any("coop_active=1 navis=2" in ln for ln in p["marker"]):
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} has no '[NETPLAY] coop_active=1 navis=2' marker")
            ok = False
        if p["distinct_navi"] < args.min_distinct_navi:
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} navi hash took {p['distinct_navi']} distinct values "
                  f"(want >= {args.min_distinct_navi}: gameplay, not a title screen)")
            ok = False
        for navi in (0, 1):
            n, path, far = p["travel"].get(navi, (0, 0.0, 0.0))
            if far < args.min_travel:
                print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} captain {navi} moved at most {far:.1f} from its first position "
                      f"(want >= {args.min_travel})")
                ok = False
    if h["travel"] != j["travel"]:
        print("run_pair: FAIL: the captains' positions differ between the peers")
        ok = False
    if args.mode == "vs":
        ok = check_vs(h, j, args) and ok
    return ok


def check_vs(h, j, args):
    ok = True
    for name, p in (("host", h), ("join", j)):
        if not p["vs_over"]:
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} logged no '[VS] match over' line")
            ok = False
        if not args.vs_no_score and not p["vs_score"] and not any(re.search(r"pieces [1-9]|pieces \d+ - [1-9]", ln) for ln in p["vs_over"]):
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} recorded no scoring")
            ok = False
        if p["distinct_mode"] < 3:
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} VS mode column took {p['distinct_mode']} distinct values")
            ok = False
        if p["vs_matches"] < args.vs_matches:
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} started {p['vs_matches']} VS matches (want >= {args.vs_matches})")
            ok = False
        if args.vs_matches >= 2 and not any("rematch" in ln for ln in p["vs_end"]):
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} has no rematch line")
            ok = False
    for key in ("vs_over", "vs_end", "vs_score"):
        if [ln.strip() for ln in h[key]] != [ln.strip() for ln in j[key]]:
            # The end screen line names who confirmed; the same text on both.
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: the peers' {key} lines differ")
            ok = False
    if ok:
        print("run_pair: VS: same match results, scoring and end-screen choices on both peers, on the same ticks")
    return ok


def launcher_run_dir(run):
    dirs = sorted((run / "netplay").glob("run-*")) if (run / "netplay").is_dir() else []
    return dirs[-1] if dirs else None


EXT_KINDS = {
    "input": re.compile(r"navi=(\d) input ext="),
    "rotate": re.compile(r"navi=(\d) input ext=0x[0-9a-f]+ rotate=-?[1-9]"),
    "bomb": re.compile(r"navi=(\d) bomb command"),
    "lock": re.compile(r"navi=(\d) lock acquired"),
    "charge": re.compile(r"navi=(\d) charge started"),
    "release": re.compile(r"navi=(\d) charge released"),
    "explode": re.compile(r"bomb exploded"),
}


def ext_lines(text):
    return [ln.strip() for ln in text.splitlines() if ln.startswith("[EXT]")]


def check_ext(h, j, args):
    """The sim's [EXT] trace: the same lines on both peers, and every
    --require-ext kind on both (per captain except explode)."""
    ok = True
    hl, jl = ext_lines(h["text"]), ext_lines(j["text"])
    if hl != jl:
        first = next((i for i, (x, y) in enumerate(zip(hl, jl)) if x != y), min(len(hl), len(jl)))
        print(f"run_pair: FAIL: the peers' [EXT] lines differ ({len(hl)} vs {len(jl)}, first at line {first})")
        ok = False
    else:
        print(f"run_pair: [EXT] lines identical on both peers ({len(hl)} lines)")
    navis = [int(n) for n in args.require_ext_navis.split(",") if n.strip()]
    for kind, rx in EXT_KINDS.items():
        counts = {}
        for ln in hl:
            m = rx.search(ln)
            if m:
                key = int(m.group(1)) if m.groups() else "any"
                counts[key] = counts.get(key, 0) + 1
        print(f"run_pair: [EXT] {kind}: " + (", ".join(f"navi {k}: {v}" if k != "any" else f"{v}"
                                                      for k, v in sorted(counts.items(), key=str)) or "none"))
        if kind in args.require_ext:
            need = ["any"] if kind == "explode" else navis
            missing = [n for n in need if not counts.get(n)]
            if missing:
                print(f"run_pair: FAIL: [EXT] {kind} missing for {missing}")
                ok = False
    for kind in ("bomb", "lock", "charge", "release", "rotate", "explode"):
        sample = [ln for ln in hl if EXT_KINDS[kind].search(ln)][:2]
        for ln in sample:
            print(f"run_pair:   {ln}")
    return ok


def check_desync(h, j, args):
    ok = True
    for name, p in (("host", h), ("join", j)):
        run = args.out / name
        if p["rc"] != 5:
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} exit={p['rc']} (want 5)")
            ok = False
        if not p["desync"]:
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} logged no 'desync detected' line")
            ok = False
        fdir = launcher_run_dir(run) if args.ice else run
        report = fdir / "desync-report.txt" if fdir else None
        if report is None or not report.exists():
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} wrote no desync-report.txt")
            ok = False
            continue
        text = report.read_text(errors="replace")
        peer = "join" if name == "host" else "host"
        two_sided = f"desync subs {name} " in text and f"desync subs {peer} " in text
        print(f"run_pair: {name}: {report} ({len(text.splitlines())} lines, "
              f"{'both sides' if two_sided else 'ONE SIDE ONLY'})")
        for ln in text.splitlines():
            if "first differing tick" in ln or "differs:" in ln or "objects at tick" in ln:
                print(f"run_pair: {name}:   {ln.strip()}")
        if not two_sided:
            ok = False
        log = fdir / "session-inputs.pknl"
        if not log.exists():
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} has no session input log {log}")
            ok = False
    return ok


def check_refuse(h, j):
    ok = True
    for name, p in (("host", h), ("join", j)):
        if p["rc"] != 4 or not p["refused"]:
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} exit={p['rc']} refused lines={len(p['refused'])} (want exit 4 and a "
                  "'handshake refused:' line)")
            ok = False
        if p["started"]:
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: {name} started a session")
            ok = False
    return ok


def exe_variant(exe, run):
    """A copy of exe with one byte appended: same code, different SHA-256."""
    run.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    dst = run / ("variant-" + Path(exe).name)
    shutil.copyfile(exe, dst)
    with open(dst, "ab") as f:
        f.write(b"\0")
    return dst


def ice_env(args):
    env = dict(PIKMIN_NETPLAY_NO_CLIPBOARD="1", PIKMIN_NETPLAY_BANNER_MS="0",
               PIKMIN_NETPLAY_ICE_TIMEOUT_MS=str(int(min(args.timeout, 1800) * 1000)))
    if args.stun != "default":
        env["PIKMIN_NETPLAY_STUN"] = args.stun
    if args.ice_bind != "any":
        env["PIKMIN_NETPLAY_ICE_BIND"] = args.ice_bind
    if args.turn:
        env["PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TURN"] = args.turn
    return env


def wait_for_file(path, proc, timeout):
    deadline = time.time() + timeout
    while time.time() < deadline:
        if path.exists() and path.stat().st_size > 0:
            return True
        if proc is not None and proc.poll() is not None:
            return False
        time.sleep(0.2)
    return False


def ice_host_args(run):
    return ["--netplay-host-ice", "--netplay-code-out", str(run / "offer.txt"),
            "--netplay-answer-in", str(run / "answer-in.txt"), "--netplay-run-root", str(run / "netplay")]


def ice_join_args(run, offer):
    return ["--netplay-join-ice", "@" + str(offer), "--netplay-code-out", str(run / "answer.txt"),
            "--netplay-run-root", str(run / "netplay")]


def clear_codes(run):
    for stale in ("offer.txt", "answer.txt", "answer-in.txt"):
        if (run / stale).exists():
            (run / stale).unlink()


def free_udp_port(preferred):
    for port in [preferred] + list(range(preferred + 1, preferred + 50)):
        s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)
        try:
            s.bind(("127.0.0.1", port))
            return port
        except OSError:
            continue
        finally:
            s.close()
    raise SystemExit("run_pair: no free UDP port")


def main(argv=None):
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    p.add_argument("--exe", type=Path, required=True, help="netplay game executable")
    p.add_argument("--exe-join", type=Path, default=None, help="joiner executable (default --exe)")
    p.add_argument("--exe-join-variant", action="store_true",
                   help="give the joiner a copy of --exe with one byte appended (exe mismatch test)")
    p.add_argument("--assets", type=Path, required=True, help="extracted game files (the directory holding dataDir/)")
    p.add_argument("--ticks", type=int, required=True)
    p.add_argument("--out", type=Path, required=True, help="private output directory")
    p.add_argument("--port", type=int, default=48810)
    p.add_argument("--seed-host", type=int, default=101, help="host input generator seed")
    p.add_argument("--seed-join", type=int, default=202, help="joiner input generator seed")
    p.add_argument("--netplay-seed", type=int, default=1, help="PIKMIN_NETPLAY_SEED (both)")
    p.add_argument("--delay", default="2", help="PIKMIN_NETPLAY_DELAY (frames or auto)")
    p.add_argument("--config", nargs="*", default=[], metavar="key=value", help="settings for both peers")
    p.add_argument("--config-host", nargs="*", default=[], metavar="key=value")
    p.add_argument("--config-join", nargs="*", default=[], metavar="key=value")
    p.add_argument("--env", nargs="*", default=[], metavar="K=V", help="extra environment for both")
    p.add_argument("--env-host", nargs="*", default=[], metavar="K=V")
    p.add_argument("--env-join", nargs="*", default=[], metavar="K=V")
    p.add_argument("--latency-ms", type=float, default=0.0, help="in-exe one-way latency (GekkoNet channel)")
    p.add_argument("--jitter-ms", type=float, default=0.0)
    p.add_argument("--loss-pct", type=float, default=0.0)
    p.add_argument("--proxy", default=None, metavar="LAT:JIT:LOSS",
                   help="route the joiner through netplay_impair_proxy with this impairment")
    p.add_argument("--proxy-exe", type=Path, default=None, help="netplay_impair_proxy (default next to --exe)")
    p.add_argument("--expect", choices=("sync", "refuse", "desync"), default="sync")
    p.add_argument("--desync-nudge", default=None, metavar="FRAME[:KIND[:ORD]]",
                   help="TEST ONLY: the joiner moves one object (piki|navi|teki, default piki 0) at FRAME "
                        "(PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_DESYNC_NUDGE)")
    p.add_argument("--ice", action="store_true", help="connect over ICE with codes exchanged through files")
    p.add_argument("--stun", default="none", help="--ice: PIKMIN_NETPLAY_STUN: none (the default), public, host:port, or default (leave it unset)")
    p.add_argument("--ice-bind", default="127.0.0.1", help="--ice: PIKMIN_NETPLAY_ICE_BIND (or any)")
    p.add_argument("--turn", default=None, help="--ice: PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TURN host:port:user:pass")
    p.add_argument("--offer", type=Path, default=None, help="--peer-only join --ice: the host's offer file")
    p.add_argument("--min-distinct-navi", type=int, default=100)
    p.add_argument("--min-travel", type=float, default=50.0, help="world units each captain must move")
    p.add_argument("--throttled", action="store_true", help="run at the real 30 Hz pace")
    p.add_argument("--timeout", type=float, default=900)
    p.add_argument("--peer-only", choices=("host", "join"), default=None,
                   help="run one peer against --remote (two-PC test)")
    p.add_argument("--remote", default=None, help="joiner: host ip:port")
    p.add_argument("--bind", default="127.0.0.1", help="PIKMIN_NETPLAY_UDP_BIND for --peer-only")
    p.add_argument("--mode", choices=("coop", "vs"), default="coop", help="session mode (--netplay-mode)")
    p.add_argument("--vs-map", type=Path, default=None, help="--mode vs: a map.json for both peers (--vs-map)")
    p.add_argument("--vs-map-join", type=Path, default=None, help="--mode vs: the joiner's own --vs-map")
    p.add_argument("--vs-starts", default="130,2135", help="--mode vs: script control starts (session ticks)")
    p.add_argument("--vs-yaw-host", type=int, default=4187,
                   help="--mode vs: host control yaw (faces its near small piece on impact_arena)")
    p.add_argument("--vs-yaw-join", type=int, default=36955, help="--mode vs: joiner control yaw (the same, turned 180)")
    p.add_argument("--vs-path", default="85:-15:96,38:26:92,3:0:96", help="--mode vs: walk legs (gen_inputs --vs-path)")
    p.add_argument("--vs-swarm", default="0:0", help="--mode vs: gen_inputs --vs-swarm")
    p.add_argument("--vs-tap", default="12:18", help="--mode vs: gen_inputs --vs-tap")
    p.add_argument("--vs-tap-windows", default="126:400,1790:1000000", help="--mode vs: gen_inputs --vs-tap-windows")
    p.add_argument("--vs-tap-windows-join", default=None, help="--mode vs: the joiner's own tap windows")
    p.add_argument("--vs-matches", type=int, default=1, help="--mode vs, --expect sync: matches that must start")
    p.add_argument("--ext", action="store_true", help="seeded ext events on both peers (gen_inputs --ext)")
    p.add_argument("--ext-events", default=None, help="explicit ext events for both (gen_inputs --ext-events)")
    p.add_argument("--ext-events-host", default=None)
    p.add_argument("--ext-events-join", default=None)
    p.add_argument("--require-ext", default="", help="ext kinds that must take effect: " + ",".join(EXT_KINDS))
    p.add_argument("--require-ext-navis", default="0,1", help="captains that must show each --require-ext kind")
    p.add_argument("--gen-args", default="", help="extra gen_inputs.py arguments for both (one string)")
    p.add_argument("--gen-args-host", default="")
    p.add_argument("--gen-args-join", default="")
    p.add_argument("--vs-no-score", action="store_true", help="--mode vs: a match without scoring still passes")
    a = p.parse_args(argv)

    a.out = a.out.resolve()
    assets = a.assets.resolve()
    if not (assets / "dataDir").is_dir():
        raise SystemExit(f"run_pair: {assets} has no dataDir/")
    shared_env = dict(PIKMIN_NETPLAY_SEED=str(a.netplay_seed), PIKMIN_NETPLAY_DELAY=a.delay)
    if a.mode == "vs":
        shared_env["PIKMIN_NETPLAY_DEBUG_VS"] = "1"
    if a.latency_ms or a.jitter_ms or a.loss_pct:
        shared_env.update(PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_LATENCY_MS=str(a.latency_ms),
                          PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_JITTER_MS=str(a.jitter_ms),
                          PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_LOSS_PCT=str(a.loss_pct))
    if a.ice:
        shared_env.update(ice_env(a))
    shared_env.update(parse_kv(a.env, "env"))
    config = parse_kv(a.config, "config")
    mode_args = {"host": [], "join": []}
    gen_extra = {"host": None, "join": None}
    if a.mode == "vs":
        for role in ("host", "join"):
            vs_map = a.vs_map_join if role == "join" and a.vs_map_join else a.vs_map
            mode_args[role] = ["--netplay-mode", "vs"] + (["--vs-map", str(vs_map.resolve())] if vs_map else [])
            gen_extra[role] = ["--vs-starts=" + a.vs_starts, "--vs-path=" + a.vs_path, "--vs-swarm=" + a.vs_swarm,
                               "--vs-tap=" + a.vs_tap, "--vs-tap-windows=" + (a.vs_tap_windows_join if role == "join" and a.vs_tap_windows_join else a.vs_tap_windows),
                               "--vs-yaw=" + str(a.vs_yaw_host if role == "host" else a.vs_yaw_join)]
    else:
        a.vs_matches = 0
    for role in ("host", "join"):
        extra = a.gen_args.split() + (a.gen_args_host if role == "host" else a.gen_args_join).split()
        if extra:
            gen_extra[role] = (gen_extra[role] or []) + extra
    a.require_ext = [k for k in a.require_ext.split(",") if k.strip()]
    a.ext_on = bool(a.ext or a.ext_events or a.ext_events_host or a.ext_events_join)
    if a.ext_on:
        shared_env["PIKMIN_NETPLAY_DEBUG_EXT"] = "1"
        for role in ("host", "join"):
            extra = ["--ext"] if a.ext else []
            events = (a.ext_events_host if role == "host" else a.ext_events_join) or a.ext_events
            if events:
                extra.append("--ext-events=" + events)
            gen_extra[role] = (gen_extra[role] or []) + extra
    if a.desync_nudge is not None:
        a.env_join = list(a.env_join) + ["PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_KNOBS=1",
                                         f"PIKMIN_NETPLAY_TEST_DESYNC_NUDGE={a.desync_nudge}"]

    if a.peer_only:
        role = a.peer_only
        run = a.out / role
        cfg = dict(config, **parse_kv(a.config_host if role == "host" else a.config_join, "config"))
        pkni = prepare_run(run, assets, cfg, a.ticks, a.seed_host if role == "host" else a.seed_join, gen_extra[role])
        if a.ice:
            clear_codes(run)
            if role == "host":
                args = ice_host_args(run)
            else:
                if not a.offer or not a.offer.exists():
                    raise SystemExit("run_pair: --peer-only join --ice needs --offer <the host's offer.txt>")
                args = ice_join_args(run, a.offer.resolve())
        elif role == "host":
            args = ["--netplay-host", str(a.port)]
        else:
            if not a.remote:
                raise SystemExit("run_pair: --peer-only join needs --remote <host-ip>:<port>")
            args = ["--netplay-join", a.remote]
        env = dict(shared_env, PIKMIN_NETPLAY_UDP_BIND=a.bind,
                   **parse_kv(a.env_host if role == "host" else a.env_join, "env"))
        print(f"run_pair: {role}: exe={a.exe.resolve()} sha256={sha256_file(a.exe)} bind={a.bind}")
        proc, out = launch(a.exe, run, args + mode_args[role] + ["--netplay-input", str(pkni)], env, not a.throttled,
                           a.ticks)
        print(f"run_pair: {role}: pid {proc.pid}, log {run / 'native.log'}")
        if a.ice and role == "host":
            if wait_for_file(run / "offer.txt", proc, 120):
                print(f"run_pair: host: offer written to {run / 'offer.txt'}; put the joiner's answer in "
                      f"{run / 'answer-in.txt'}")
            else:
                print("run_pair: host: no offer was written")
        elif a.ice:
            if wait_for_file(run / "answer.txt", proc, 120):
                print(f"run_pair: join: answer written to {run / 'answer.txt'}; copy it to the host's answer-in.txt")
            else:
                print("run_pair: join: no answer was written")
        rcs = wait_all([(role, proc)], a.timeout)
        out.close()
        info = peer_summary(role, run, rcs[role])
        print(f"HASH_LOG={run / 'hashes.txt'}")
        ok = rcs[role] == 0 and info["ticks"] == a.ticks and not info["desync"]
        print(f"run_pair: {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'} (single peer; compare hashes.txt with the other PC's)")
        return 0 if ok else 1

    if a.ice and a.proxy:
        raise SystemExit("run_pair: --proxy is UDP only")
    port = free_udp_port(a.port)
    exe_host = a.exe
    exe_join = a.exe_join or a.exe
    if a.exe_join_variant:
        exe_join = exe_variant(a.exe, a.out / "join")
    host_run, join_run = a.out / "host", a.out / "join"
    host_pkni = prepare_run(host_run, assets, dict(config, **parse_kv(a.config_host, "config")), a.ticks, a.seed_host,
                            gen_extra["host"])
    join_pkni = prepare_run(join_run, assets, dict(config, **parse_kv(a.config_join, "config")), a.ticks, a.seed_join,
                            gen_extra["join"])
    print(f"run_pair: host exe={Path(exe_host).resolve()} sha256={sha256_file(exe_host)}")
    print(f"run_pair: join exe={Path(exe_join).resolve()} sha256={sha256_file(exe_join)}")

    procs = []
    files = []
    join_target = port
    if a.proxy:
        lat, jit, loss = (a.proxy.split(":") + ["0", "0", "0"])[:3]
        proxy_exe = a.proxy_exe
        if proxy_exe is None:
            # The build puts the tool in the build root, the game in bin/.
            near = [d / "netplay_impair_proxy.exe" for d in (Path(a.exe).resolve().parent,
                                                             Path(a.exe).resolve().parent.parent)]
            proxy_exe = next((c for c in near if c.exists()), near[0])
        join_target = free_udp_port(port + 1)
        plog = open(a.out / "proxy.log", "w")
        files.append(plog)
        proxy = subprocess.Popen([str(proxy_exe), "--listen", str(join_target), "--upstream", str(port),
                                  "--bind", "127.0.0.1", "--lat", lat, "--jit", jit, "--loss", loss,
                                  "--seed", "7", "--run-seconds", str(int(a.timeout))],
                                 stdout=plog, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
        print(f"run_pair: proxy pid {proxy.pid} :{join_target} -> :{port} lat={lat} jit={jit} loss={loss}")
        time.sleep(0.5)
    loop_env = dict(shared_env, PIKMIN_NETPLAY_UDP_BIND="127.0.0.1")
    if not a.ice and a.expect == "desync":
        # UDP runs keep their forensics in the run directory.
        loop_env["PIKMIN_NETPLAY_INPUT_LOG"] = "session-inputs.pknl"
    join_own = dict(config, **parse_kv(a.config_join, "config"))
    if a.ice:
        clear_codes(host_run)
        clear_codes(join_run)
        host_args = ice_host_args(host_run)
    else:
        host_args = ["--netplay-host", str(port)]
    hproc, hout = launch(exe_host, host_run, host_args + mode_args["host"] + ["--netplay-input", str(host_pkni)],
                         dict(loop_env, **parse_kv(a.env_host, "env")), not a.throttled, a.ticks)
    procs.append(("host", hproc))
    files.append(hout)
    if a.ice:
        if not wait_for_file(host_run / "offer.txt", hproc, 120):
            print("run_pair: FAIL: the host wrote no offer code")
            wait_all(procs, 5)
            return 1
        print(f"run_pair: offer code: {host_run / 'offer.txt'} ({(host_run / 'offer.txt').stat().st_size} B)")
        join_args = ice_join_args(join_run, host_run / "offer.txt")
    else:
        time.sleep(0.5)
        join_args = ["--netplay-join", f"127.0.0.1:{join_target}"]
    jproc, jout = launch(exe_join, join_run, join_args + mode_args["join"] + ["--netplay-input", str(join_pkni)],
                         dict(loop_env, **parse_kv(a.env_join, "env")), not a.throttled, a.ticks)
    procs.append(("join", jproc))
    files.append(jout)
    if a.ice:
        if not wait_for_file(join_run / "answer.txt", jproc, 120):
            print("run_pair: FAIL: the joiner wrote no answer code")
            wait_all(procs, 30)
            return 1
        shutil.copyfile(join_run / "answer.txt", host_run / "answer-in.tmp")
        os.replace(host_run / "answer-in.tmp", host_run / "answer-in.txt")
        print(f"run_pair: answer code: {join_run / 'answer.txt'} -> {host_run / 'answer-in.txt'}")
    print(f"run_pair: host pid {hproc.pid}{'' if a.ice else f' :{port}'}, join pid {jproc.pid}")
    start = time.time()
    rcs = wait_all(procs, a.timeout)
    secs = time.time() - start
    if a.proxy:
        proxy.kill()  # our own child only
        proxy.wait(timeout=30)
    for f in files:
        f.close()
    print(f"run_pair: both peers done in {secs:.1f}s")
    h = peer_summary("host", host_run, rcs["host"])
    j = peer_summary("join", join_run, rcs["join"])
    if a.ice:
        for name, info in (("host", h), ("join", j)):
            for ln in lines_with(info["text"], "[netplay] ice transport ready") + lines_with(info["text"], "adopted the host"):
                print(f"run_pair: {name}:   {ln.strip()}")
    if a.expect == "sync":
        ok = check_sync(h, j, a)
        if a.ext_on or a.require_ext:
            ok = check_ext(h, j, a) and ok
    elif a.expect == "desync":
        ok = check_desync(h, j, a)
    else:
        ok = check_refuse(h, j)
    if a.ice and join_own:
        # Adoption is for the session only: the joiner's file keeps its own values.
        on_disk = {}
        conf = join_run / "pikmin_settings.conf"
        for ln in (conf.read_text(errors="replace").splitlines() if conf.exists() else []):
            if "=" in ln and not ln.lstrip().startswith("#"):
                k, v = ln.split("=", 1)
                on_disk[k.strip()] = v.strip()
        kept = {k: on_disk.get(k) for k in join_own}
        if all(str(v) == kept[k] for k, v in join_own.items()):
            print(f"run_pair: the joiner's settings file keeps its own values {kept}")
        else:
            print(f"run_pair: FAIL: the joiner's settings file has {kept}, want its own {join_own}")
            ok = False
    print(f"run_pair: {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'} (expect {a.expect})")
    return 0 if ok else 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main())
